<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Sun, 22 Nov 2026 04:13:12 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>希尔玛·阿夫·克林特 (Hilma af Klint) 的一幅极其罕见的抽象画作在拍卖会上以 1,270 万美元的创纪录价格售出。但它到底应该打折吗？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/one-of-hilma-al-klint-amazingly-rare-abstract-painting-sold-for-a-record-12-million-at-auctionbut-should-it-have-been-on-sale-at-all-180989922/</link><description>1920 年创作的《Ser III No. 5》以预售估价近 16 倍的价格售出后，批评者指责阿芙·克林特希望将她的“神圣作品”集中保存在一座寺庙中，而不是分散在私人收藏中</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:23:48 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/one-of-hilma-al-klint-amazingly-rare-abstract-painting-sold-for-a-record-12-million-at-auctionbut-should-it-have-been-on-sale-at-all-180989922/</guid></item><item><title>这座拥有 2000 年历史的古墓中出土的一个罗马杯子和数百件其他宝藏揭示了古代亚洲帝国丰富的交换网络</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-roman-cup-and-hundreds-other-treasures-unearthed-in-this-2000-year-old-tomb-reveal-the-rich-exchange-network-of-an-ancient-asian-empire-180989920/</link><description>匈奴人统治中亚约300年。现在，在蒙古发现的一座坟墓揭示了田园文化与罗马帝国、汉族和乐浪郡的联系</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:22:42 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-roman-cup-and-hundreds-other-treasures-unearthed-in-this-2000-year-old-tomb-reveal-the-rich-exchange-network-of-an-ancient-asian-empire-180989920/</guid></item><item><title>伦勃朗的《夜巡》充满生机。研究人员揭示了这件杰作中隐藏的微生物世界</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/rembrandt-night-watch-is-teeming-with-life-researchers-reveal-a-hidden-world-of-microbes-all-over-the-masterpiece-180989917/</link><description>从这幅 17 世纪画作中采集的样本揭示了无数微生物，其中包括 2013 年在日本一家糖厂首次发现的一种令人费解的细菌</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:21:53 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/rembrandt-night-watch-is-teeming-with-life-researchers-reveal-a-hidden-world-of-microbes-all-over-the-masterpiece-180989917/</guid></item><item><title>天文学家首次目睹巨星吞噬其较小的恒星伴星</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-the-first-time-astronomers-witnessed-a-giant-star-gobble-up-its-smaller-stellar-companion-180989905/</link><description>这次合并在 2025 年底引发了一次喷发，研究人员急忙使用几台地面和太空望远镜记录了这次喷发。利用较旧的数据和计算机模拟的帮助，该团队重建了整个天体物理过程</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:21:50 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/for-the-first-time-astronomers-witnessed-a-giant-star-gobble-up-its-smaller-stellar-companion-180989905/</guid></item><item><title>一群孤立的亚马逊狩猎采集者罕见地向外界寻求帮助，引发了对森林退化的担忧</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-isolated-group-of-amazonian-hunter-gatherers-made-a-rare-request-for-help-from-outsiders-raising-concerns-about-forest-degradation-180989909/</link><description>大约 20 名土著阿瓦部落成员从雨林中走出来，从邻近村民那里领取食物。该组织几十年来没有与外界联系，因此专家表示，森林砍伐可能使这些人别无选择</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:08:26 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/an-isolated-group-of-amazonian-hunter-gatherers-made-a-rare-request-for-help-from-outsiders-raising-concerns-about-forest-degradation-180989909/</guid></item><item><title>九磅重的老鹰似乎在非洲猎杀 60 磅重的狒狒——暗示掠食者也可能追捕我们的祖先</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nine-pound-eagles-seem-to-be-hunting-60-pound-baboons-in-africa-hinting-the-predators-may-have-gone-after-our-ancestors-too-180989906/</link><description>在乍得东北部，研究人员发现了维罗鹰攻击成年橄榄狒狒的证据，这些狒狒的体重与一个小人一样重。研究结果表明，早期人类必须提防来自天空的伏击，这可能影响了他们的进化</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nine-pound-eagles-seem-to-be-hunting-60-pound-baboons-in-africa-hinting-the-predators-may-have-gone-after-our-ancestors-too-180989906/</guid></item><item><title>在中国两个洞穴中发现的牙齿正在改写直立人的故事，直立人是一种远古人类祖先，其能力可能比我们想象的还要强大</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/teeth-discovered-in-two-chinese-caves-are-rewriting-the-story-of-homo-erectus-an-ancient-human-ancestor-that-may-have-been-more-capable-than-we-thought-180989913/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，该物种在亚洲大陆的存在时间比之前认为的要长 216,000 年。另一位研究人员表示，另一种说法是直立人能够生活在热带雨林中，这一发现“颠覆了”常见的灭绝理论。</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:10:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/teeth-discovered-in-two-chinese-caves-are-rewriting-the-story-of-homo-erectus-an-ancient-human-ancestor-that-may-have-been-more-capable-than-we-thought-180989913/</guid></item><item><title>乔治亚·欧姬芙以绘画花卉和沙漠而闻名。为什么我们忘记了她对美国建筑的痴迷？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/georgia-okeeffe-is-famous-for-painting-flowers-and-deserts-why-have-we-forgotten-her-obsession-with-american-architecture-180989911/</link><description>底特律艺术学院举办的新展览展出了近 40 件艺术品，重点展示了艺术家对建筑环境（从乡村农舍到城市摩天大楼）的迷人描绘</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/georgia-okeeffe-is-famous-for-painting-flowers-and-deserts-why-have-we-forgotten-her-obsession-with-american-architecture-180989911/</guid></item><item><title>心爱的河马菲奥娜在吞下不小心扔进动物园围栏的孩子帽子后死亡</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-child-tossed-a-hat-and-a-ceiling-fan-sent-it-flying-into-a-hippos-zoo-enclosure-where-the-animal-ate-it-heres-how-the-care-team-is-responding-180989894/</link><description>动物护理团队最初乐观地认为辛辛那提动物园的网红河马能够自然排出物体并康复，但情况最终变成了“医疗紧急情况”</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:21:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-child-tossed-a-hat-and-a-ceiling-fan-sent-it-flying-into-a-hippos-zoo-enclosure-where-the-animal-ate-it-heres-how-the-care-team-is-responding-180989894/</guid></item><item><title>哈佛归还两个可能属于被奴役者的头骨，150 多年来，这些头骨是从巴西运来用于优生学研究的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/harvard-returns-two-skulls-likely-belonging-to-enslaved-individuals-more-than-150-years-after-they-were-taken-from-brazil-for-eugenics-studies-180989910/</link><description>在研究人员、社区团体和巴西政府多年的压力下，遗骸在里约热内卢和萨尔瓦多举行了隆重的仪式欢迎归来。一个头骨可能属于一位在 1835 年奴隶起义中战斗并死亡的人</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:22:56 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/harvard-returns-two-skulls-likely-belonging-to-enslaved-individuals-more-than-150-years-after-they-were-taken-from-brazil-for-eugenics-studies-180989910/</guid></item><item><title>观看在英格兰切斯特动物园出生的稀有小犀牛，这是对其脆弱物种的可爱促进</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-rare-baby-rhinoceros-born-in-englands-chester-zoo-an-adorable-addition-to-its-species-numbers-180989902/</link><description>这头小牛出生于 10 月 11 日，健康状况良好，正在与母亲一起探索一个僻静的围场，远离公众视线</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:18:05 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-rare-baby-rhinoceros-born-in-englands-chester-zoo-an-adorable-addition-to-its-species-numbers-180989902/</guid></item><item><title>美国国立卫生研究院决定明年将最后一批退休研究黑猩猩转移到动物保护区</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-nih-has-decided-to-move-its-last-group-of-retired-research-chimpanzees-to-an-animal-sanctuary-next-year-180989907/</link><description>该机构此前已确定这些动物年龄太大或患病，不适合此次旅行。但最近涉及另一个联邦政府支持的研究机构的转移促使美国国立卫生研究院重新审视这个问题</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:35:25 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-nih-has-decided-to-move-its-last-group-of-retired-research-chimpanzees-to-an-animal-sanctuary-next-year-180989907/</guid></item><item><title>考古学家最终拼凑出古希腊最大的谜团之一“帕台农神庙之谜”吗？</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/have-archaeologists-finally-pieced-together-the-parthenon-puzzle-one-of-ancient-greece-greatest-mysteries-180989903/</link><description>几个世纪前，帕台农神庙的东山墙已化为废墟。德国研究人员现在相信，在罗马石棺和 3D 打印机的帮助下，他们已经重现了描绘雅典娜诞生的 39 幅人物场景</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 19:06:45 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/have-archaeologists-finally-pieced-together-the-parthenon-puzzle-one-of-ancient-greece-greatest-mysteries-180989903/</guid></item><item><title>这款自动充电牙刷的刷毛可以发电，帮助杀死导致蛀牙和牙龈疾病的细菌</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-self-charging-toothbrush-has-bristles-that-generate-electricity-to-help-kill-bacteria-that-cause-cavities-and-gum-disease-180989895/</link><description>在一项简短的临床试验中，使用实验牙刷的参与者报告说，与使用传统尼龙毛刷的参与者相比，牙菌斑、牙龈炎症和出血更少。然而，需要更多的研究来评估该工具的安全性和有效性</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-self-charging-toothbrush-has-bristles-that-generate-electricity-to-help-kill-bacteria-that-cause-cavities-and-gum-disease-180989895/</guid></item><item><title>这位哲学家是第一批将自己的遗体捐献给科学的人之一。近 200 年后，研究人员仍在从中学习</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/he-was-one-of-the-first-people-to-donate-his-body-to-science-nearly-200-years-later-researchers-are-still-learning-from-it-180989901/</link><description>功利主义创始人杰里米·边沁 (Jeremy Bentham) 的尸体被公开解剖，并变成了一个“自动图标”，这是一个栩栩如生的展示，展示了他穿着一套西装的骷髅</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:31:07 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/he-was-one-of-the-first-people-to-donate-his-body-to-science-nearly-200-years-later-researchers-are-still-learning-from-it-180989901/</guid></item><item><title>北大西洋露脊鲸数量锐减，引发人们对这一极度濒危物种未来的担忧</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-north-atlantic-right-whale-population-has-shrunk-raising-concerns-about-the-future-of-the-critically-endangered-species-180989896/</link><description>大型海洋哺乳动物因船只撞击、渔具缠结和其他原因而死亡，这影响了该物种数量增长的能力。大约100年前，这些动物被猎杀至濒临灭绝</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/the-north-atlantic-right-whale-population-has-shrunk-raising-concerns-about-the-future-of-the-critically-endangered-species-180989896/</guid></item><item><title>现代法医调查揭示了在北爱尔兰沼泽中发现的 2000 年前尸体的死因</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-modern-forensic-investigation-reveals-the-cause-of-death-of-a-2000-year-old-body-found-in-an-bog-in-northern-ireland-180989898/</link><description>考古学家与验尸官合作确定，“Ballymacoms More Woman”在似乎是铁器时代的祭祀仪式中被斩首时只有 15 至 22 岁</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:36:20 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-modern-forensic-investigation-reveals-the-cause-of-death-of-a-2000-year-old-body-found-in-an-bog-in-northern-ireland-180989898/</guid></item><item><title>从尼安德特人遗传的基因变异可能会影响现代人类的大脑大小并提供预防精神分裂症的保护</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-gene-variant-inherited-from-neanderthals-might-affect-modern-humans-brain-size-and-provide-protection-against-schizophrenia-180989893/</link><description>一项新的研究表明，当今世界上大约 20% 的欧洲血统的人至少携带一个该变体的副本。它与较小的枕叶（处理视觉信息的区域）有关，并且可使患精神分裂症的风险降低近 10%</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:57:10 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-gene-variant-inherited-from-neanderthals-might-affect-modern-humans-brain-size-and-provide-protection-against-schizophrenia-180989893/</guid></item><item><title>中世纪的读者将洪水、瘟疫和彗星视为末日的预兆，因此他们创作了一本神秘的世界末日艺术品手稿以供随意阅读</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/medieval-readers-saw-floods-plagues-and-comets-as-omens-of-doom-so-they-created-a-mysterious-manuscript-of-apocalyptic-artworks-to-peruse-at-will-180989891/</link><description>《奇迹之书》是一本可能创作于奥格斯堡的 16 世纪手稿，即将拍卖。它有 167 幅描绘极端天气事件和奇怪天象的画作</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:53:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/medieval-readers-saw-floods-plagues-and-comets-as-omens-of-doom-so-they-created-a-mysterious-manuscript-of-apocalyptic-artworks-to-peruse-at-will-180989891/</guid></item><item><title>就在这幅弗里达·卡罗 (Frida Kahlo) 的画作有望以 350 万美元的价格售出之前几个小时，它就被从拍卖会上拍了下来</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/hours-before-it-was-expected-to-sell-for-up-to-3-million-this-frida-kahlo-painting-was-whisked-from-the-auction-block-180989890/</link><description>据称，这幅 1952 年的画作“Congreso de los pueblos por la paz”在可疑的情况下从卡罗位于墨西哥城的博物馆中消失了。遗产组织认为它理应属于墨西哥公众</description><pubDate>Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:30:48 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/hours-before-it-was-expected-to-sell-for-up-to-3-million-this-frida-kahlo-painting-was-whisked-from-the-auction-block-180989890/</guid></item></channel></rss>